lesson k-growing-things v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=5 subject=nature levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Growing things"
  goal "Say the order a bean grows in, count petals and flowers, and say that a seed needs water to sprout."

  look {
    scene 28x14 {
      growstages grow stages=4 numbers=true names=1 at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      A bean starts as a seed in the soil. With water and warmth it sends up a shoot, then it grows
      leaves, and at last it flowers. It happens in that order every time.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.grow-next s=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.grow-next count=2 seed=2
    practice k.petals count=2 seed=3
    practice k.count-flowers count=2 seed=4 easy-count=1
    show k.dry-dish d=1
    practice k.bee-visits count=1 seed=6
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.seeds-in-the-dark
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.bean-weeks k=1 easy-k=0 hard-k=2
  }
  remember {
    say "Seed, shoot, leaves, flower. A seed needs water to grow."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. The seeds in the dark are a surprise to most adults too: a seed
    carries its own food, so it sprouts without light, though it grows pale and needs light soon
    after. If the child is stuck on the order, ask what the bean has now and what it has not got
    yet. Off the page, put a bean on wet kitchen paper in a jar and look at it every day for a week.
    Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines), 環境, 内容 (5): "身近な動植物に親しみをもって接し，生命の尊さに気付き，いたわったり，大切にしたりする。"
    (Treat familiar animals and plants with affection, notice that life is precious, and care for it.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the first stage after the seed is found in the teacher's pen, the flowers have three or four petals, and the three-star asks for two weeks."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the bean is further on, the flowers have six to eight petals, and the three-star counts weeks from the seed or the shoot to the flower."
  }
}
